"content_hash":"b88e91c9df168271fb7d4232f3c740021a64f97bcfc24df6cf6d58a490c6bd9b","event_uuid":"acae8313-89bb-4b26-a796-d483656ba62c","position":{"commit_sha":"4353f0b92f34f071b129f34bbd7c560d452694d0","position":"1789703915344857226-acae8313-89bb-4b26-a796-d483656ba62c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"6af276156f8538efb2c94bf4fa2ab1646319e8b0b0685afad04f3b91714e75b0","event_uuid":"8faa03b9-1b7f-489a-a9c7-205d55d56832","position":{"commit_sha":"c5c625a03686da2b87d42e35b03a2fca4f2af1fe","position":"1789703936105578532-8faa03b9-1b7f-489a-a9c7-205d55d56832"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"8fd6b1a271a7d6fb84d44c7d020101141aa60f5d723211f0eaca75446a3e2764","event_uuid":"92bde950-bfb4-401d-90ad-8a8a1790d786","position":{"commit_sha":"92a2994ea575010993dded640a2d93bca6ea454c","position":"1789708896419353430-92bde950-bfb4-401d-90ad-8a8a1790d786"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d220136b8e84143d328d170bfa326b05b7548c8c2add56d66c1ad23908171419","event_uuid":"658cb810-6caa-4d24-99b9-3154dd3f53f2","position":{"commit_sha":"90ad37ecac0a4d3dbd7a53a6fc1c74214b208958","position":"1789709076546786491-658cb810-6caa-4d24-99b9-3154dd3f53f2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"8984e5ad8729572cb33d098b86720abb3181efaa0b3db5adbad483010fc549d6","event_uuid":"54f771f5-d443-4043-a3b4-3d26a646bbff","position":{"commit_sha":"0a52c2d04ae306bf454b4ca1556ee7963668c1eb","position":"1789709150104439378-54f771f5-d443-4043-a3b4-3d26a646bbff"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"4c94eef2bb5cc6ae9fc73880dedf51fa819abbda1eeef232dadb1cdc5253c1d3","event_uuid":"9905d162-b473-4831-98dd-11d5f161a592","position":{"commit_sha":"0a52c2d04ae306bf454b4ca1556ee7963668c1eb","position":"1789709150129926794-9905d162-b473-4831-98dd-11d5f161a592"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1789703915344857226,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8faa03b9-1b7f-489a-a9c7-205d55d56832","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ce66-59ef-d6d7-4c7a"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nA commit that changes a **function body inside `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`** is\ninstalled on the box but never applied to the containers that function creates. The\nchange appears deployed by every marker autodeploy keeps, while the running container\nis built from the previous body. No subsequent tick corrects it.\n\nConfirmed in production while deploying `ce66-59ef-d6d7-4c7a`.\n\n## Observed behaviour\n\n`ce66` added 3 `-e` flags and 1 `-v` bind to `mcp_run_new()` in\n`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`, and the matching settings to\n`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`.\n\nAfter the merge tick completed and reported success:\n\n- `/opt/rebar/infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` **did** contain the new flags and bind.\n- `/var/lib/rebar/deployed-sha`, `mcp-deployed-sha`, and `bot-deployed-sha` all read\n  the merged commit.\n- autodeploy logged `mcp redeployed + healthy` and `deploy complete: env now reflects\n  <merged sha>`.\n- The live container `rebar-mcp-<sha>-8093` had **none** of the 3 env vars and **no**\n  `/var/lib/rebar` bind.\n\nEvery marker and log line reported a correct deployment of a container that did not\nhave the change.\n\n## Root cause\n\nWithin a single tick the ordering is: rsync `/opt/rebar` to the target commit, then\nperform the component rolls. The rsync replaces the script **file**, but the running\nshell continues executing the **already-parsed body** it was started with. So the roll\nthat happens after the rsync calls the *previous* `mcp_run_new`.\n\nThe next tick has the new body, but by then `mcp_deployed` has been stamped to\n`TARGET`, so `mcp_delta()` is empty and no roll occurs. The change is then permanently\nunapplied until some unrelated future commit happens to touch a path in `MCP_PATHS`.\n\nThis generalises: it affects any autodeploy function that constructs a container, not\njust `mcp_run_new`, and it is silent in every case.\n\n## Recovery performed\n\nForcing a corrective roll required resetting the **global** marker, not just the\ncomponent one. `mcp_delta()` is unreachable when `TARGET` equals `DEPLOYED`, because\nthe up-to-date branch exits before component deltas are computed. Resetting only\n`mcp-deployed-sha` produced `up to date; no-op` on every tick. Resetting\n`/var/lib/rebar/deployed-sha` **and** `mcp-deployed-sha` to the parent commit and\nstarting the unit rolled MCP correctly with the new body; the live container now\ncarries all 3 env vars and the bind, and both markers were restored automatically.\n\nThis recovery is an operator break-glass, not a fix.\n\n## Investigation notes\n\nCandidate directions, to be evaluated rather than assumed correct: re-exec the script\nfrom its installed path once after the rsync so the remainder of the tick runs the new\nbody; or make the component delta consider the deploying script's own content so a\nbody change forces a roll on the following tick; or separate \"install sources\" from\n\"perform rolls\" into two ticks. The chosen approach must be established by\ninvestigation. Any fix must not introduce a re-exec loop.\n\n`infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` documents that a commit touching *only*\n`autodeploy.sh` needs a manual install. That note is adjacent but does not describe\nthis defect: here the install happened automatically and still did not take effect.\nThe runbook should be corrected alongside the fix.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The root cause is reproduced in a test that fails before the fix, demonstrating\n      that a change to a container-constructing function in `autodeploy.sh` is not\n      reflected in the container created during the same tick; the pre-fix failure\n      output is recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] After the fix, a commit that changes only a container-constructing function body\n      in `autodeploy.sh` results in a running container built from the new body,\n      verified by asserting on the resulting container configuration and reporting the\n      assertion output.\n- [ ] The fix introduces no re-exec or redeploy loop, verified by a test that runs\n      consecutive ticks against an unchanged target and asserts exactly one roll\n      occurs, with the tick log recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] Deployment markers cannot report a component as deployed at a commit whose body\n      change was not applied, verified by a test asserting marker state against actual\n      container state.\n- [ ] `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` is updated to describe this failure mode and\n      the corrective procedure, verified by quoting the added section.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass, reported with their exit status.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"the defect: rsync replaces the script file mid-tick while the running shell keeps its already-parsed body, and the up-to-date early exit then makes mcp_delta unreachable"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"the adjacent autodeploy.sh note does not describe this failure mode or the two-marker recovery"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_body_change_2d65.py","reason":"new regression coverage: body change applied within the tick, exactly one roll on an unchanged target, markers cannot claim a component deployed at an unapplied body"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"54f771f5-d443-4043-a3b4-3d26a646bbff","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2d65-32dd-28b9-43ef","ticket_type":"bug","title":"autodeploy applies autodeploy.sh body changes one tick late, then never","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["acae8313-89bb-4b26-a796-d483656ba62c","8faa03b9-1b7f-489a-a9c7-205d55d56832","92bde950-bfb4-401d-90ad-8a8a1790d786","658cb810-6caa-4d24-99b9-3154dd3f53f2","54f771f5-d443-4043-a3b4-3d26a646bbff","9905d162-b473-4831-98dd-11d5f161a592"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789712447644711558,"uuid":"55fca402-a1e7-4f41-8585-1e457a00a0ba"}